# ECONOMICS

> The arena isn't powered by hope.
>
> It runs on incentives.

The economics of Wraith are designed around one idea:

## The arena should feed itself.

Competition creates activity.

Activity generates fees.

Fees support rewards.

Rewards create competition.

The cycle repeats.

---

# 💡 THE PHILOSOPHY

Most projects build a token and then try to find a purpose for it.

Wraith starts with a game.

A leaderboard.

A tournament.

A reward system.

The economy exists to support the arena.

Not the other way around.

---

# ⚡ THE PROTOCOL FEE

Wraith is designed around a:

## 2% Protocol Fee

The fee exists to support the infrastructure behind the arena.

The objective is not to extract value.

The objective is to sustain the ecosystem.

A healthy arena requires:

- Infrastructure
- Competition
- Rewards
- Development
- Operations

The fee helps support those components.

---

# 🔄 THE ECONOMIC LOOP

The machine is intentionally simple.

```text
PLAYERS
    ↓
ACTIVITY
    ↓
PROTOCOL FEES
    ↓
REWARD INFRASTRUCTURE
    ↓
TOURNAMENT REWARDS
    ↓
PLAYER PARTICIPATION
    ↓
MORE ACTIVITY
```

Every component supports the next.

A stronger arena creates more competition.

More competition creates more participation.

More participation strengthens the system.

---

# 🏆 WHY REWARDS MATTER

Competition without rewards creates pride.

Competition with rewards creates intensity.

The reward system exists because:

Winning should matter.

When players are competing for something tangible:

- Scores become important
- Leaderboards become meaningful
- Rivalries become real
- Tournament results become memorable

The arena works because there is something at stake.

---

# 🏦 THE REWARD ALLOCATION

A portion of ecosystem activity is designed to support the reward engine.

The exact operational configuration may evolve over time.

The purpose remains the same:

Support competitive play.

Support tournament rewards.

Support the growth of the arena.

The objective is simple:

If activity increases, the arena should be capable of benefiting from it.

---

# 🐋 THE 3% RULE

Nobody owns the arena.

The token architecture is designed around:

## MAX WALLET: 3%

The purpose is to reduce concentration and maintain a healthier competitive ecosystem.

One wallet should not become the entire room.

Three percent is already a lot.

Wraith believes you'll survive.

---

## Example

Wallet:

> "I'd like more than 3%."

Protocol:

> "No."

Wraith:

> "I agree."

---

# ⚖️ FAIRNESS

The arena is built around competition.

Competition only works if players believe the rules are applied consistently.

The economic system therefore aims to be:

- Transparent
- Predictable
- Verifiable
- Understandable

Complexity does not automatically create value.

Most of the time it just creates confusion.

Wraith prefers fewer moving parts.

---

# 📈 GROWTH

The objective is not to create the most complicated economy possible.

The objective is to create an economy that gets stronger as participation grows.

A healthy ecosystem creates:

- More activity
- More engagement
- More competition
- More rewards
- More history

Every champion contributes to that history.

Every tournament contributes to that history.

Every reward contributes to that history.

---

# 🤖 WRAITH AND THE ECONOMY

Wraith watches the economy.

Wraith reacts to the economy.

Wraith comments on the economy.

But Wraith does not control the economy.

The machine determines:

- Fees
- Rewards
- Wallet rules
- Transactions
- Distribution

Wraith talks about what happened.

Wraith does not invent what happened.

This distinction matters.

---

# 🔎 VERIFIABILITY

The arena should not depend on trust alone.

Important economic activity should be capable of being independently verified.

That includes things such as:

- Protocol configuration
- Public reward activity
- Reward-related transactions
- Wallet limitations
- Tournament outcomes

Wraith can announce events.

Verification is what makes them real.

---

# 🚫 WHAT THE ECONOMY IS NOT

The Wraith economy is not designed to be:

- A savings account
- A bank
- An investment fund
- A guaranteed income stream
- A promise of profit

The economy exists to support:

- The arena
- The game
- The tournaments
- The rewards
- The ecosystem

Nothing more.

Nothing less.

---

